# Knowledge model: family allowances for one child under the Swiss Federal Act
# on Family Allowances (Familienzulagengesetz, FamZG), version of 1 January 2026.
#
# Scope: child allowance and education allowance for one child, for one person.
# Not in scope: cantonal amounts, children abroad, several persons entitled for
# the same child (see fz:Scope).
#
# Standards: RDF, RDFS, SHACL Core, SHACL-SPARQL, SKOS, PROV-O, XSD.
# Own vocabulary: sk: (vocabulary/sk.ttl).
#
# Conventions:
# - Each question is a property shape of fz:ApplicationShape.
# - Each relevance rule (sk:RelevanceRule) gives a result when its question is
#   relevant. Answers to questions that are not relevant are not in the data.
# - Each rule (sk:Rule) gives one result per SELECT row: a refusal, a value or a
#   next step. Its sources are given with prov:wasDerivedFrom.
# - All rules read their numbers from parameters (sk:Parameter). The app adds
#   the parameter nodes to the data graph.
# - Each interpretation is an sk:Interpretation. Each open point is an
#   sk:OpenPoint. Rules that are not complete have sk:status sk:Open.
# - The results are for the calendar month of the date of the application
#   (fz:I_ApplicationMonth).

@prefix fz:   <https://github.com/almilo/software-that-knows/model/famzg#> .
@prefix sk:   <https://github.com/almilo/software-that-knows/vocabulary#> .
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix sh:   <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix prov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

fz: a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Family allowances for one child (FamZG)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Child allowance and education allowance for one child under the FamZG, version of 1 January 2026."@en ;
    owl:imports sk: ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom fz:FamZG .

fz:Scope a sk:OpenPoint ;
    rdfs:label "Scope"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Not in the model: cantonal amounts (FamZG Art. 3 para. 2), birth and adoption allowances, children who live abroad (FamZG Art. 4 para. 3), several persons entitled for the same child (FamZG Art. 6 and 7)."@en .

